enabled. Under the LGPL 2.1 option, distributors of resulting binaries are
expected to either:

  (a) provide the recipient with the means to relink the binary against a
      modified libspatialite (typically by shipping the .o files of all
      modules that link directly with libspatialite, or by providing the
      shpx source code so the recipient can rebuild), or
  (b) license the resulting binary under MPL 1.1 or GPL 2.0 instead.

Distributors should consult the LGPL 2.1 text for the exact requirements.
shpx itself is dual-licensed MIT OR Apache-2.0; combining it with the
bundled libspatialite via static linking puts the resulting binary under
the additional terms of one of the libspatialite licenses (per recipient
choice).

================================================================================
PROJ (transitively bundled via shpx-geom + proj-sys)
================================================================================

When the `bundled-spatialite` feature is enabled, libspatialite is linked
against libproj 9.4.x, which is built from C source by the `proj-sys` crate
(via the `shpx-geom/bundled-proj` feature, which `bundled-spatialite` implies).

PROJ is licensed under the X/MIT License (a permissive, BSD-style license).
The full PROJ license text is shipped inside the proj-sys crate's vendored
PROJ source tree (under the `LICENSE` file).

shpx does not vendor PROJ source directly; it consumes whichever PROJ version
proj-sys 0.25.0 (or compatible) builds. See `crates/shpx-geom/Cargo.toml`
for the exact `proj` / `proj-sys` versions in use.

================================================================================
shpx local modifications to libspatialite 5.1.0 source tree
================================================================================

Removed (not vendored, present in upstream tarball):

   - `test/`, `examples/` — test data and sample programs, not needed for shpx.
   - autotools generated files (`aclocal.m4`, `configure`, `config.*`,
     `Makefile.*`, `m4/`) — replaced by shpx's `build.rs`.
   - `src/srsinit/epsg_inlined_{00..63,prussian}.c` (12 MB total) — full EPSG
     seed data, not needed when `OMIT_EPSG` is defined. Only the WGS84 seed
     files (`epsg_inlined_wgs84_00.c`, `epsg_inlined_wgs84_01.c`) and the
     dispatcher (`epsg_inlined_extra.c`) are kept.
   - `src/srsinit/epsg_update/` — upstream maintainer-only code generator.
   - `src/connection_cache/generator/`, `src/gaiageo/lemon/`,
     `src/gaiageo/flex/` — upstream-only code generators (we ship the already
     generated `Kml.c` / `Gml.c` / etc. as part of the source tree).

The vendored C source itself is bit-identical to the upstream tarball.
